    Bug 2060601 - Fix heap-buffer-overflow in nsParseMailMessageState::FinalizeHeaders() by using HeaderData::length instead of treating header slices as NUL-terminated C strings. r=jtracey

    HeaderData::value is a (pointer, length) slice into the shared m_headers buffer. It is only NUL-terminated when the parser encounters a trailing CR/LF for that header. If the final header in a block has no terminating newline, value is not NUL-terminated, but FinalizeHeaders() and InternSubject() treat it as a C string anyway (via nsDependentCString, strlen-based APIs, and unbounded PL_strchr/PL_strstr/PL_strcasestr), resulting in reads beyond the end of the buffer.

    Fix: Replace each such use with length-bounded equivalents nsCString(value, length) instead of nsDependentCString(value), PL_strnchr/PL_strnstr/PL_strncasestr instead of their unbounded counterparts, and copy into a local nsAutoCString before calling APIs that require a true NUL-terminated C string (e.g., PR_ParseTimeString and NS_MsgGetPriorityFromString).

    Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316542

